2026-06-09 15:48:52,694 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: To address the requirements for strict GDPR compliance, data protection, and sovereignty of data within the European Union, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can implement several security measures and regulatory compliance strategies based on our existing capabilities. 

Firstly, as we have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed and our standard data residency is set to EU only, we ensure that all personal data is stored and processed within the European Union, adhering to the sovereignty of data requirement. Our cross-border transfer policy prohibits transfers outside the EU unless there's an explicit legal basis, further reinforcing GDPR compliance.

To protect personal data, we can utilize our anonymisation tools, including Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models, to ensure that no personal data is used in training pipelines without proper anonymization. We also have experience with implementing data subject rights such as access, rectification, erasure, portability, and objection, which are crucial for GDPR compliance.

Our data protection impact assessment (DPIA) capability allows us to assess the potential risks associated with processing personal data and implement appropriate measures to mitigate these risks. With an average DPIA duration of 3 weeks, we can efficiently conduct these assessments as part of our project workflow.

Furthermore, we enforce multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), ensuring secure access to systems and data. Our role-based access control (RBAC) design experience enables us to implement fine-grained access controls, limiting access to personal data to only those who need it for their tasks.

In terms of network security, our zero-trust architecture, micro-segmentation, and defense-in-depth approach provide robust protection against unauthorized access. We also have intrusion detection and prevention systems (IDS/IPS) deployed, which are regularly updated and monitored.

For audit and logging purposes, all queries are logged with an append-only mechanism using SHA-256 hash chaining for immutability. This ensures that any attempts to tamper with logs would be detectable, supporting our compliance efforts.

Lastly, we have experience with regulatory frameworks such as GDPR, RGS v2 (ANSSI), SecNumCloud, and others, which positions us well to navigate the complex landscape of data protection regulations within the EU.

By leveraging these capabilities and strategies, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can ensure that our solution not only meets but exceeds the necessary standards for GDPR compliance, data sovereignty, and protection, thereby guaranteeing the security and integrity of personal data processed within our systems.
